You'll tame a dog, cat or horse, peaceful or hostile, by throwing it any
food it can eat (I think there's an exception for dogs when there's a
full moon). Any food a domestic creature can't eat (like tins, or meaty
corpses thrown to herbivores or fruit thrown to carnivores) will make it
peaceful (probably sees your good intentions). In a fight with lots of
creatures, it's often a good idea to throw whatever food you have at dogs
and cats and horses to make them not want to attack you.

There's special code to prevent thrown food actually hitting a critter and
making it hostile when it's already peaceful, so you don't have to worry
about that.

When critters are *already* tame, they'll only eat their own kind of food
unless they're really really hungry.

